message: "If you use G-Frames in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "G-Frames: overlap-driven video frame selection for photogrammetry"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23674120
repository-code: "https://github.com/aymenaiblu/G-Frames"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23674120
    description: "Zenodo archive of release v1.1.0"
url: "https://www.aymenaiblu.com"
abstract: >-
  G-Frames is a native macOS application that converts video of any length into a
  photogrammetry-ready image set. It measures camera motion (pyramidal Lucas-Kanade
  optical flow with forward-backward checking) and image sharpness for every analysed
  frame, then selects the smallest set of sharp frames that keeps a target overlap
  between consecutive views. It masks people (Apple Vision) and burned-in overlays,
  reprojects 360-degree video into perspective views, and writes a COLMAP-ready folder
  with full provenance. Developed for remote heritage documentation of the Old Town of
  Ghadames (Libya).
keywords:
  - photogrammetry
  - structure from motion
  - keyframe selection
  - video
  - cultural heritage
  - COLMAP
  - Ghadames
  - macOS
